## Verdict: challenge, P2

The ordinary-PR fixes named by T are present, but the owner's veto can still be left unenforced when the exact revert's workflow has terminated without producing its required check. In warrant/gate.py:1514-1518, approve_held subtracts every required workflow that has any run at the revert head, ignoring that run's status and conclusion. A completed cancelled run therefore suppresses all future dispatches although check_reasons still reports CHECK_MISSING. enforce_brakes:1565-1573 also skips the merge because this exact revert is already pending. Repeated gate passes make no recovery write, so the unchanged revert stays blocked indefinitely without outside intervention. This is a missing-check recovery failure, not a request to waive red checks or merge without CI.

The controlled fixture below constructs a real merge of AGENTS.md under a brake, a signed fixture actor's timely veto, and the exact revert in a separate fixture Git repository. The actual gate assessment recognizes facts.revert and refuses it only for CHECK_MISSING. Its simulated GitHub API reports a completed/cancelled workflow_dispatch run for the required workflow at exactly that revert head, and no check runs. Two passes through the actual enforce_brakes and approve_held make no recovery write. Controls: the same exact revert with no workflow run dispatches CI; a queued run is correctly left alone. GitHub documents cancellation of queued workflows (https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/manage-workflow-runs/cancel-a-workflow-run) and reports completed/cancelled runs through its run-list API (https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/workflow-runs?apiVersion=2022-11-28). The missing-check state is supplied by the fixture; no live GitHub cancellation experiment was made and no live veto is claimed to have been lost.

Expected: recover a terminal workflow that cannot produce the missing required check, while preserving the green-check requirement and leaving active runs alone. A fix belongs in an ordinary constitutional pull request with a regression case and a mutant, under D's stated procedure.

